   174	that equality holds.  More precisely, any taut filling of $X(\sigma)$ is a
   175	simplicial chain whose support complex is clean and triangulates $B^3$; the
   176	resulting triangulation is freely shellable and flag.  The key input is the
   177	general fact that taut fillings of integral $n$-cycles split under disjoint
   178	union, connected sum, and more generally under almost disjoint union, where
   179	the summands are supported on vertex sets meeting in at most $n+1$ vertices.
   180	\end{abstract}
